#!/usr/bin/env python
"""
Subgroup (age x race/ethnicity) evaluation of the four EchoNext SHD models.

Models supported (pass any subset; omitted ones are skipped):
    --early-bayes  PATH   Pyro early-fusion (FiLM) Bayesian CNN   (earlyfusion_pyro_checkpoint.pt)
    --late-bayes   PATH   Pyro late-fusion Bayesian CNN           (latefusion_pyro_checkpoint.pt)
    --early-cnn    PATH   Deterministic early-fusion (FiLM) CNN   (state_dict or checkpoint dict)
    --late-cnn     PATH   Deterministic late-fusion CNN           (state_dict or checkpoint dict)

For every model the script reports, for the chosen split (default: test), overall and for
every age group, race/ethnicity group and age x race/ethnicity intersection cell:
    n, SHD prevalence, accuracy (+95% Wilson CI), sensitivity, specificity, AUROC

For the two Bayesian models it additionally splits each group into INCONCLUSIVE vs CONCLUSIVE
ECGs, using the same rule as find_inconclusive_patients.py (95% interval of the posterior draws
straddles the threshold AND >= 20% of draws lie on the other side) and reports the share of
inconclusive ECGs and the accuracy within each part, plus the ECGs that are inconclusive under
BOTH Bayesian models. (The deterministic CNNs have no posterior, so this is not defined for them.)
Outputs: long/wide CSVs, age x race matrices and a Markdown report.

Example
-------
python subgroup_evaluation.py \
    --data-dir ../EchoNextData \
    --early-bayes earlyfusion_pyro_results/earlyfusion_pyro_checkpoint.pt \
    --late-bayes  latefusion_pyro_results/latefusion_pyro_checkpoint.pt \
    --early-cnn   earlyfusion_cnn.pt \
    --late-cnn    latefusion_cnn.pt \
    --out-dir subgroup_results      # add --threshold 0.5 --minority-frac 0.2 --mc-samples 200 (defaults)

SECURITY NOTE: checkpoints are loaded with torch.load(weights_only=False) because the
Pyro checkpoints contain sklearn objects / pandas indices. Only load files you created.
"""

